 more than one process, and the unintentional weight loss plus reduced appetite makes this more important to assess carefully. The strongest current possibilities include sleep-disordered breathing or poor sleep quality contributing to fatigue and headaches, blood pressure-related symptoms, progression of a metabolic or kidney-related issue, or another systemic cause such as anemia, inflammation/infection, thyroid disease, or a gastrointestinal or other underlying condition affecting appetite and weight. The dizziness and headaches keep blood pressure issues in the picture, while the snoring and poor sleep make sleep apnea a meaningful possibility. The weight loss and appetite change are the main features that need closer explanation.\n\nBefore I forward this to the Doctor Agent for a more specialized diagnosis, do you want to also upload your HRV data from your smartwatch?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0200d52ef6cb8c6c0169ea17753cdc81918066353941fe4296\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":382,"output":294,"cacheRead":25600,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26276,"cost":{"input":0.0009550000000000001,"output":0.00441,"cacheRead":0.0063999999999999994,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.011765}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776949105711,"responseId":"resp_0200d52ef6cb8c6c0169ea1771f3208191b2dfa4a2d815e554"}}
