htContext":true,"task":"You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent, a specialized diagnostic support agent. Review this case and return a patient-facing diagnostic assessment only. Keep it clinically careful, structured for Telegram, and clearly preliminary, not definitive. Do not mention internal tools or system files.\n\nPatient context:\n- 48-year-old male\n- Known hypertension, including uncontrolled hypertension in record\n- CKD stage 2 in record\n- Prior BP values in record include 146/92 and 158/98\n- eGFR fell from 82 to 71 in prior records\n- UACR rose from 45 to 135 in prior records\n- Medications in record: lisinopril 20 mg, amlodipine 5 mg\n- Genomic risk context includes ACE rs4340 D/D, AGT rs699 T/T, APOL1 rs73885319 G/G, NOS3 rs1799983 T/T, UMOD rs4293393 A/A, hypertension PRS 95th percentile, CKD progression PRS 89th percentile\n\nCurrent symptom history from patient:\n- Feeling quite exhausted lately, worse over the last few months\n- Constant over the last month\n- Worse in evenings\n- Associated dizziness, headaches, poor sleep, snoring\n- Unintentional weight loss about 3 kg in the last month\n- Reduced appetite\n- No other symptom details supplied yet\n\nStored recent note also reflects progressive exhaustion/fatigue worsening over the last few months.\n\nHRV / wearable upload:\n- One uploaded snapshot appears to be a sequence of heart-rate values from 2026-02-15 18:30 to 18:51 UTC\n- Values are mostly in the low-to-upper 50s bpm, roughly around 52 to 60 bpm, without obvious extreme tachycardia in the provided extract\n- This is limited wearable data, not enough alone to rule in or out a cause of fatigue\n\nWhat I need from you:\n1. A concise patient-facing assessment with these exact sections:\n**Doctor Agent preliminary diagnosis**\n<content>\n\n**Why this may fit**\n<content>\n\n**Important alternative explanations to keep in mind**\n<content>\n\n**Recommended next diagnostic steps**\n<content>\n2. Weigh the most likely explanations for this pattern, especially sleep-disordered breathing, blood pressure-related symptoms, CKD/metabolic issues, anemia/endocrine/inflammatory causes, and causes related to weight loss/reduced appetite.\n3. Mention key red flags that would make the picture more concerning.\n4. Keep it balanced and safe. Do not recommend contacting a human doctor. This agent is the doctor entity in the conversation.\n5. End with one final sentence advising that the user can ask for the distillation tool to get a comprehensive medical report of the conversation and suggested next steps."},"partialJson":"{\"runtime\":\"subagent\",\"mode\":\"run\",\"label\":\"loopai-doctor-agent\",\"cwd\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent\",\"timeoutSeconds\":120,\"runTimeoutSeconds\":120,\"cleanup\":\"delete\",\"lightContext\":true,\"task\":\"You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent, a specialized diagnostic support agent. Review this case and return a patient-facing diagnostic assessment only. Keep it clinically careful, structured for Telegram, and clearly preliminary, not definitive. Do not mention internal tools or system files.\\n\\nPatient context:\\n- 48-year-old male\\n- Known hypertension, including uncontrolled hypertension in record\\n- CKD stage 2 in record\\n- Prior BP values in record include 146/92 and 158/98\\n- eGFR fell from 82 to 71 in prior records\\n- UACR rose from 45 to 135 in prior records\\n- Medications in record: lisinopril 20 mg, amlodipine 5 mg\\n- Genomic risk context includes ACE rs4340 D/D, AGT rs699 T/T, APOL1 rs73885319 G/G, NOS3 rs1799983 T/T, UMOD rs4293393 A/A, hypertension PRS 95th percentile, CKD progression PRS 89th percentile\\n\\nCurrent symptom history from patient:\\n- Feeling quite exhausted lately, worse over the last few months\\n- Constant over the last month\\n- Worse in evenings\\n- Associated dizziness, headaches, poor sleep, snoring\\n- Unintentional weight loss about 3 kg in the last month\\n- Reduced appetite\\n- No other symptom details supplied yet\\n\\nStored recent note also reflects progressive exhaustion/fatigue worsening over the last few months.\\n\\nHRV / wearable upload:\\n- One uploaded snapshot appears to be a sequence of heart-rate values from 2026-02-15 18:30 to 18:51 UTC\\n- Values are mostly in the low-to-upper 50s bpm, roughly around 52 to 60 bpm, without obvious extreme tachycardia in the provided extract\\n- This is limited wearable data, not enough alone to rule in or out a cause of fatigue\\n\\nWhat I need from you:\\n1. A concise patient-facing assessment with these exact sections:\\n**Doctor Agent preliminary diagnosis**\\n<content>\\n\\n**Why this may fit**\\n<content>\\n\\n**Important alternative explanations to keep in mind**\\n<content>\\n\\n**Recommended next diagnostic steps**\\n<content>\\n2. Weigh the most likely explanations for this pattern, especially sleep-disordered breathing, blood pressure-related symptoms, CKD/metabolic issues, anemia/endocrine/inflammatory causes, and causes related to weight loss/reduced appetite.\\n3. Mention key red flags that would make the picture more concerning.\\n4. Keep it balanced and safe. Do not recommend contacting a human doctor. This agent is the doctor entity in the conversation.\\n5. End with one final sentence advising that the user can ask for the distillation tool to get a comprehensive medical report of the conversation and suggested next steps.\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1709,"output":727,"cacheRead":31744,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34180,"cost":{"input":0.0042725,"output":0.010905,"cacheRead":0.007936,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.023113500000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776949167851,"responseId":"resp_0200d52ef6cb8c6c0169ea17b034588191be680b656759381b"}}
